dict(p="""Most of us check our phones dozens of times a day, often without any clear reason. Technology companies design apps to be habit-forming. Features such as endless scrolling and unpredictable notifications work like slot machines, offering small rewards at random times. Because we never know when something interesting will appear, we keep checking. Breaking this habit requires changing the environment rather than relying on willpower alone. Turning off non-essential notifications, keeping the phone in another room while studying, and setting specific times for social media can all [weaken|strengthen] the automatic urge to check. The goal is not to give up technology but to <use it on our own terms>.""",
m=[('요지', ['습관적인 휴대 전화 사용은 의지보다 환경을 바꾸어 통제해야 한다.', '의지력만 있으면 스마트폰 중독을 쉽게 끊을 수 있다.', '앱의 알림 기능은 사용자에게 꼭 필요하다.', '기술을 완전히 포기해야 집중할 수 있다.', '스마트폰은 슬롯머신보다 위험하지 않다.']),
   ('제목', ['Take Back Control of Your Phone', 'Why Notifications Are Always Useful', 'Willpower Solves Everything', 'Slot Machines in History', 'Living Without Technology'])],
b=['let companies decide for us', 'check it more often', 'give up the internet completely'],
s=("Apps are designed to form habits through ___(A)___ rewards, so changing our ___(B)___ helps reduce automatic checking.", [('random', 'environment'), ('regular', 'environment'), ('random', 'password'), ('large', 'phone'), ('fixed', 'friends')]),
x='앱은 무작위 보상으로 습관을 만들므로 환경을 바꾸어 기술을 주도적으로 써야 한다.'),
